# RAG Java Lab - Processing Pipeline

## Overview

The processing pipeline is responsible for transforming an uploaded document into searchable vector embeddings.

Rather than storing an uploaded file directly for AI retrieval, the system performs several processing stages:

1. Store the original file.
2. Extract readable text.
3. Split the text into smaller chunks.
4. Generate embeddings for each chunk.
5. Store the vectors in PostgreSQL using pgvector.
6. Activate the processed document version.

This pipeline ensures that every uploaded document becomes searchable using semantic similarity.

